async function triggerDR() {
  await promoteGlobalWriter('us-west-2');
  await updateRoute53Records('us-west-2');
  await validateFailover();
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ABAC, cross-account trust, per-tenant encryption, and test rigor for production-grade data lakes.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC with IAM tags and S3 object tags
- Per-tenant KMS CMKs and encryption context
- Cross-account role with least privilege
- Test plan including canaries and revocation

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::telemetry-lake/tenant-id=${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}/*"
      ],
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "s3:ExistingObjectTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["kms:Decrypt","kms:Encrypt","kms:GenerateDataKey*"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:kms:region:acct:key/<tenant-id-CMK-arn>",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "kms:EncryptionContext:tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical ability to apply basic AWS guardrails in a real-world multi-team setup.

## Key Concepts

- IAM least privilege with per-prefix access
- S3 bucket policy enforcement for encryption and public access
- Event-driven validation with Lambda on PutObject
- Observability via CloudWatch

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal Lambda skeleton to validate encryption and prefix
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const r = event.Records[0];
  const bucket = r.s3.bucket.name;
  const key = r.s3.object.key;
  const enc = r.s3.object.serverSideEncryption;
  if (!enc) throw new Error("Object not encrypted");
  if (!/^corp-logs\/team-(a|b|c)\//.test(key)) throw new Error("Wrong prefix");
  return;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale this pattern for more teams?
- How would you test revocation and auditing of access?
